.TH SDL_SetRenderScale 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_SetRenderScale \- Set the drawing scale for rendering on the current target.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_render.h>
.PP
.BI "bool SDL_SetRenderScale(SDL_Renderer *renderer, float scaleX, float scaleY);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The drawing coordinates are scaled by the x/y scaling factors before they are used by the renderer\[char46] This allows resolution independent drawing with a single coordinate system\[char46]
.PP
If this results in scaling or subpixel drawing by the rendering backend, it will be handled using the appropriate quality hints\[char46] For best results use integer scaling factors\[char46]
.PP
Each render target has its own scale\[char46] This function sets the scale for the current render target\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I renderer
the rendering context\[char46]
.TP
.I scaleX
the horizontal scaling factor\[char46]
.TP
.I scaleY
the vertical scaling factor\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns true on success or false on failure; call
.BR SDL_GetError ()
for more information\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
This function should only be called on the main thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_GetRenderScale (3)
